 "bs_mb_tall_kneel_scoop": "Tall-kneel, both knees down. Scoop medicine ball overhead into wall. Extension without hips — abs and thoracic only. One rep is one full, controlled movement from start to finish and back.",
 "bs_mb_to_free_swing_complex": "You need a medicine ball, your game bat and a batting tee. 1 hard med-ball rotational shot-put, then immediately 2 max-intent gamer-bat swings off a tee. Rest between rounds. One rep is one full swing.",
 "bs_mb_walking_windup_toss": "You need a medicine ball. 6–8 lb med ball. Take a walking approach, wind up on the back hip, and rip into the wall. Rhythm > force. One rep is one full, controlled movement from start to finish and back.",
 "bs_ohp_carry_walk": "Kettlebell overhead, walk forward slowly with intentional micro-rotations at hips. Do NOT let the kettlebell drift. One rep is one full, controlled movement from start to finish and back.",
 "bs_overload_bat_swings_v2": "You need a heavier-than-normal bat. Use a bat 10–20% heavier than your gamer. Take controlled, high-intent dry swings from your normal stance and swing path. Same load sequence: hips, then hands. Do not muscle it — keep the barrel path identical to your gamer. One rep is one full swing.",
 "bs_pallof_iso_hold": "Cable at chest, arms extended, resist the pull. Hold 20- each side. Ribs down, glutes on. Hold the position for the prescribed number of seconds; that is one rep. Do every rep on one side, then switch sides.",
 "bs_plyo_ball_wall_rebounds": "You need a plyo ball. Set up in your hitting posture, not a throwing posture. 1–2 lb ball rebounded off the wall with the rotational pattern of a swing — hips lead, hands follow. Rapid catch-and-return, no pause, 6–. One rep is one full, controlled movement from start to finish and back.",
 "bs_pushpull_rot_complex": "3 landmine punches each side. Rest. Then 3 gamer swings. cluster rest. One rep is one full swing.",
 "bs_pvc_overspeed_swings": "Grab a light PVC pipe cut to gamer length. Take max-intent full swings — chase the loudest ‘whoosh’ at the point of contact. One rep is one full swing.",
 "bs_reactive_lead_leg_block": "On a slick pad or turf. Take stride, land with lead leg firm, immediately rotate torso — teach the leg to brace, not collapse. One rep is one full, controlled movement from start to finish and back.",
 "bs_rear_hip_shift_drill": "Stance-wide. Slow shift into rear hip — feel weight over the middle of rear foot. Return. No swing, just load. One rep is one full, controlled movement from start to finish and back.",
 "bs_rfess_pallof": "Split-squat with rear foot on bench. Cable at chest, arms extended, hold in split-squat position. One rep is one full, controlled movement from start to finish and back. Do every rep on one side, then switch sides.",
 "bs_side_plank_rot_reach": "Side plank. Top arm reaches under and through, then rotates open toward ceiling. One rep is one full, controlled movement from start to finish and back. Do every rep on one side, then switch sides.",
 "bs_sledgehammer_tire_swings": "Sledgehammer (6-12 lb) into a tire. Alternate sides. Explosive downward strike — hips lead, obliques snap the handle. One rep is one full swing.",
 "bs_speed_stick_dry_swings": "You need a speed stick. Use a Momentus Speed Trainer / Speed Stick (or similar overspeed trainer). Full-intent dry swings from your gamer stance. Listen for the whoosh at the point of contact — that is your target zone. One rep is one full swing.",
 "bs_split_squat_to_rot_throw": "Pause split-squat iso at bottom (rear foot elevated). Then 3 rotational medicine ball throws. 90s rest. One rep is one throw. Do every rep on one side, then switch sides.",
 "bs_split_stance_iso_hold": "Split stance, cable at chest resisting rotation. Hold rotated position 5-. Feel obliques + rear glute fire. Hold the position for the prescribed number of seconds; that is one rep. Do every rep on one side, then switch sides.",
 "bs_stride_drive_wall": "Rear leg against wall, lead leg strides. Push off wall into stride landing — no swing, just drive-and-land. One rep is one full, controlled movement from start to finish and back.",
 "bs_tall_kneel_antirot_press": "Both knees on floor, cable at chest, press out and hold. Removes legs — pure anti-rotational trunk. One rep is one full, controlled movement from start to finish and back. Do every rep on one side, then switch sides.",
 "bs_trapbar_jump_to_swing": "3 trap-bar jumps at 30-40% 1RM. Rest. Then 3 gamer dry swings at max intent. Rest between clusters. One rep is one full swing.",
 "bs_trapbar_to_mb_toss_complex": "You need a trap bar, weight plates and a medicine ball. 2 trap-bar jumps at ~30% 1RM, rest, then 1 hard rotational med-ball toss per side. 3–. Lower body first, then rotation. One rep is one full, controlled movement from start to finish and back.",
 "bs_underload_bat_swings_v2": "You need a lighter-than-normal bat. Take a bat 10–20% lighter than your gamer. Swing MAX intent — chase bat-speed PRs. Same swing shape you always take, just faster. If mechanics break down, rest. One rep is one full swing.",
 "bs_underload_composite_tee": "Underload bat (2-4 oz below gamer) into a tee. Full-intent swings chasing exit velo. Same swing decisions as your gamer, higher output. One rep is one full swing.",
 "bs_underload_wood_top_hand": "Light wood bat, top-hand only, off a tee at inside pitch. Palm-up finish; barrel stays connected to shoulder plane. One rep is one full swing.",
 "bs_weighted_sleeve_dry_swings": "You need your game bat. Slide a weighted training sleeve (Axe/Fungo style) onto your gamer bat. Take 3–5 dry swings emphasizing full extension through contact. Keep barrel on plane; do not shorten the path. One rep is one full swing.",
 "bs_weighted_wristwrap_swings": "Add 1-2 lb wrist wraps. Take gamer bat, dry swings. Feel forearms + hands stay quiet, hips lead. One rep is one full swing.",
 "bs_whiffle_bat_overspeed_tee": "You need a batting tee. Very light whiffle/thin-handle bat into a tee. Chase max exit velo on the whiffle ball. Same swing shape as your gamer — do not get handsy just because it is light. One rep is one full swing.",
 "build_up_sprint": "Perform the Build Up Sprint with smooth, controlled form. One rep is one run of the prescribed distance at the effort shown; walk back slowly to rest.",
 "bulgarian_split_squat": "You need two dumbbells and a bench. Perform the Bulgarian Split Squat with smooth, controlled form. One rep is one full, controlled movement from start to finish and back. Do every rep on one side, then switch sides.",
 "bulgarian_ss": "You need one dumbbell and a bench. Rear foot on bench, front shin vertical, drop straight down. One rep is one full, controlled movement from start to finish and back. Do every rep on one side, then switch sides.",
 "butcher_block_stretch": "You need a bench. Perform the Butcher Block Stretch with smooth, controlled form. Hold the position for the prescribed number of seconds; that is one rep.",
 "cable_chops": "Set the cable (or a band tied to a post) high, above your head, on one side and hold the handle with both hands. Pull it down and across your body past the opposite knee, turning from the hips; return slowly. Do every rep on one side, then switch.",
 "cable_high_low_rotation": "Set the cable (or a band tied to a post) at hip height on one side and hold the handle with both hands at your chest. Stand sideways to the anchor; turn your hips and chest away from it, pause, then return slowly. Do every rep on one side, then switch.",
